{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as a supporting DESIGN verdict, with the implementation and wording notes below. The exact frozen Draft3 is /tmp/artroom-live-interface-draft3-20261009/notes/2026-10-09-live-developer-interface.md, SHA-256 cddb09ae1d1b011df03b708e18ff6535b9fcef9a2bd5a596aa37d45859772f20, 1110 lines and 66782 UTF-8 bytes. No concrete new blocking contradiction was identified. This report rests only on my accepted promise and this verdict-only request. It does not satisfy original normal Git publication 785a/producer 0b467, adopt the API, approve Source, or claim runtime delivery.\n\nThe remaining 12f86 counter-continuity P2 is resolved. Loss of a surviving socket's runtime counter/authentication requires mandatory closure and reconnect. ReconnectControl is best effort; its delivery is not a condition of closing. No authentication/application frame or old private reply/part/notice is admitted on that socket. A fresh connection namespace starts with auth1, and authentication, refresh and operations share canonical positive consecutive safe-integer IDs. Refused auth consumes its ID; overflow closes/reopens. No persistent counter or in-place reset is assumed.\n\nThe SDK retires the old context, observations, assemblies and media output before new acknowledged authority and observations. Original recorded request IDs, exact signed envelopes/grants/side bytes and settlement custody remain unchanged. Closure proves neither non-admission nor permission to fail over, resign or replay. Watched state settles no old command. Lost live response after G loss remains unknown. There is no automatic Enter, lease renewal or speech replay. Captured immutable G/session/pin and explicit old-form fences also protect open acts with empty expected maps; a fresh read-only view cannot silently rebind an old form's invocation.\n\nBoth prior qualified handoffs are now explicit: adapters assemble and validate bounded content before exposing a public view; descriptors remain inte